Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• model_score."name": identify the problem.  
• model_score."version": keep versions aligned with solution.  
• model_score."step": limit to steps 1, 2 and 3.  
• model_score."model": detect the “Stack” model and “non‑Stack” models.  
• model_score."test_score": compare model performances.  
• solution."name": count how many times each problem appears in the solution table.  

Typical conditions that may be needed  
• model_score."step" IN (1,2,3)  
• model_score."model" LIKE '%Stack%' (for the stacker)  
• model_score."model" NOT LIKE '%Stack%' (for every other model)  
• HAVING MAX(CASE WHEN …) < MAX(CASE WHEN …) to be sure the best “non‑Stack” test score is lower than the “Stack” test score for the same (name,version,step).  


Below are ten exploratory SQL queries (each different and limited to 20 rows) that gradually build up to the final answer.

```sql
-- 1. List every distinct model name to see how “Stack” is spelled
SELECT DISTINCT "model"
FROM "model_score"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Quick look at all model‑score rows for one sample problem
SELECT *
FROM "model_score"
WHERE "name" = 'iris'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Check which steps exist in model_score
SELECT DISTINCT "step"
FROM "model_score"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Display all rows whose model contains the word “Stack”
SELECT *
FROM "model_score"
WHERE "model" LIKE '%Stack%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. For each (name,version,step) list the Stack test score
SELECT "name",
       "version",
       "step",
       MAX("test_score") AS stack_test_score
FROM   "model_score"
WHERE  "model" LIKE '%Stack%'
  AND  "step" IN (1,2,3)
GROUP  BY "name","version","step"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. For the same keys, list the best non‑Stack test score
SELECT "name",
       "version",
       "step",
       MAX("test_score") AS best_non_stack_score
FROM   "model_score"
WHERE  "model" NOT LIKE '%Stack%'
  AND  "step" IN (1,2,3)
GROUP  BY "name","version","step"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Combine the two sub‑queries and keep only rows where Stack wins
SELECT s."name",
       s."version",
       s."step",
       s.stack_test_score,
       n.best_non_stack_score
FROM   (
        SELECT "name","version","step",MAX("test_score") AS stack_test_score
        FROM   "model_score"
        WHERE  "model" LIKE '%Stack%' AND "step" IN (1,2,3)
        GROUP  BY "name","version","step"
       ) AS s
JOIN   (
        SELECT "name","version","step",MAX("test_score") AS best_non_stack_score
        FROM   "model_score"
        WHERE  "model" NOT LIKE '%Stack%' AND "step" IN (1,2,3)
        GROUP  BY "name","version","step"
       ) AS n
ON  s."name"    = n."name"
AND s."version" = n."version"
AND s."step"    = n."step"
WHERE s.stack_test_score > n.best_non_stack_score
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Count how many (name,version,step) satisfy the “Stack wins” rule
SELECT t."name",
       COUNT(*) AS cnt_stack_wins
FROM (
      -- reuse query 7 without the limit
      SELECT s."name","version","step"
      FROM (
            SELECT "name","version","step",MAX("test_score") AS stack_test_score
            FROM "model_score"
            WHERE "model" LIKE '%Stack%' AND "step" IN (1,2,3)
            GROUP BY "name","version","step"
           ) AS s
      JOIN (
            SELECT "name","version","step",MAX("test_score") AS best_non_stack_score
            FROM "model_score"
            WHERE "model" NOT LIKE '%Stack%' AND "step" IN (1,2,3)
            GROUP BY "name","version","step"
           ) AS n
      ON  s."name"    = n."name"
      AND s."version" = n."version"
      AND s."step"    = n."step"
      WHERE s.stack_test_score > n.best_non_stack_score
     ) AS t
GROUP BY t."name"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Count how many times each problem appears in the solution table
SELECT "name",
       COUNT(*) AS cnt_in_solution
FROM   "solution"
GROUP  BY "name"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final query: problems whose “Stack‑wins” count exceeds their count in solution
SELECT a."name"
FROM   (
        -- counts of stack wins
        SELECT t."name",
               COUNT(*) AS cnt_stack_wins
        FROM (
              SELECT s."name","version","step"
              FROM (
                    SELECT "name","version","step",MAX("test_score") AS stack_test_score
                    FROM "model_score"
                    WHERE "model" LIKE '%Stack%' AND "step" IN (1,2,3)
                    GROUP BY "name","version","step"
                   ) AS s
              JOIN (
                    SELECT "name","version","step",MAX("test_score") AS best_non_stack_score
                    FROM "model_score"
                    WHERE "model" NOT LIKE '%Stack%' AND "step" IN (1,2,3)
                    GROUP BY "name","version","step"
                   ) AS n
              ON  s."name"    = n."name"
              AND s."version" = n."version"
              AND s."step"    = n."step"
              WHERE s.stack_test_score > n.best_non_stack_score
             ) AS t
        GROUP BY t."name"
       ) AS a
JOIN   (
        SELECT "name",COUNT(*) AS cnt_in_solution
        FROM   "solution"
        GROUP  BY "name"
       ) AS b
ON  a."name" = b."name"
WHERE a.cnt_stack_wins > b.cnt_in_solution
LIMIT 20;
```
